<Prose title="Privacy policy" description="What OSSHunt collects: nothing beyond standard server logs. No accounts, no cookies, no tracking." updated="2026-10-23">
  <h2>Summary</h2>
  <p>OSSHunt is a static reference site. It has no accounts, forms, comments or advertising, and it does not ask you for personal information.</p>

  <h2>What the site does not do</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>It does not set cookies or use analytics, advertising or tracking scripts.</li>
    <li>It does not load third-party fonts, images or scripts, Fonts and logos are served from the site itself.</li>
    <li>Search runs in your browser against data already on the page. What you type is not sent to us.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>What the host may record</h2>
  <p>Like any web server, the hosting provider may keep standard request logs (for example IP address, requested page, time and browser type) for security and operations. We do not combine these logs with other data to identify visitors.</p>

  <h2>Email</h2>
  <p>If you write to <a href="mailto:hello@osshunt.com">hello@osshunt.com</a>, we receive your address and message and use them only to reply and to act on your request, such as a correction. We do not add you to a mailing list.</p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Pages link to vendor, project and source websites. Those sites have their own policies, and we do not control what they collect.</p>

  <h2>Data about products</h2>
  <p>The comparisons use publicly available information about software products and companies, each with a dated source. They are not personal data about visitors.</p>

  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>If this policy changes, the date above changes. To raise a question or report a concern, email <a href="mailto:hello@osshunt.com">hello@osshunt.com</a>.</p>
</Prose>
